      {
        "id": 62383,
        "name": "j1hopki1",
        "username": "j1hopki1",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/58f4c7/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-05-01T03:36:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Octavian,</p><p>I remember your variant, but I didn't comment on it when I read it because I was still working through my ideas. I'm glad you agree that he needs to be better at threatening to flip. Doesn't removing the pins mean that they never get played unless he flips?</p><p>My main problem with your Vast Following suggestion is Cursed Acolyte. In a 5 player game the first time he comes into play he deals all heroes 3 and 3 damage. Then if he dies and your Vast Following goes off it pretty much guarantees (since 5 cards will come out of the trash) that he'll come back and do another 3 and 3. That's 12 damage to all heroes from 2 cards not to mention the other 4 cards that will enter play from the Vast Following plus the next card in the deck. I think if you want to make Vast Following a guaranteed resurrection it should be H-2 cards come back.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:38:58.611Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
