        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Octavian,</p><p>I remember your variant, but I didn&#39;t comment on it when I read it because I was still working through my ideas. I&#39;m glad you agree that he needs to be better at threatening to flip. Doesn&#39;t removing the pins mean that they never get played unless he flips?</p><p>My main problem with your Vast Following suggestion is Cursed Acolyte. In a 5 player game the first time he comes into play he deals all heroes 3 and 3 damage. Then if he dies and your Vast Following goes off it pretty much guarantees (since 5 cards will come out of the trash) that he&#39;ll come back and do another 3 and 3. That&#39;s 12 damage to all heroes from 2 cards not to mention the other 4 cards that will enter play from the Vast Following plus the next card in the deck. I think if you want to make Vast Following a guaranteed resurrection it should be H-2 cards come back.</p>",
